\title{A \code{\verb~|let~} whose declared type differs from the type of its value}
\taxon{Example}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{soundness}
\tag{machine}
\meta{origin}{docs/design/review/official-divergence.md}
\import{base-macros}

\p{The official kernel types a let variable by the type the binder declares. The machine bound the variable to a value and typed the value. With [the non-transitive triple](ex-OTWJ) the two types are convertible and give different verdicts. Source: finding E1-F1 in \src{docs/design/review/official-divergence.md}, section 1, and \src{rlvm-machine/NOTES-M5.md}; [the exactness session](ses-874D).}
\pre{\verb~|
-- A, intro, h, d as in the triple
theorem S.bad : d h = 5 :=
  let q : d h = d h := Eq.refl (d intro)
  q                                          -- official: REJECT

theorem S.ok : d h = d h :=
  let q : d h = d h := Eq.refl (d intro)
  q                                          -- official: accept
~}
\ul{
\li{Officially the value \code{\verb~|Eq.refl (d intro)~} has type \code{\verb~|d intro = d intro~}, which is compared with the declared \code{\verb~|d h = d h~} and holds. The body \code{\verb~|q~} then has the declared type \code{\verb~|d h = d h~}, and that against \code{\verb~|d h = 5~} fails.}
\li{The machine gave \code{\verb~|q~} the type of its value, \code{\verb~|d intro = d intro~}, and \code{\verb~|d intro = 5~} holds: it accepted \code{\verb~|S.bad~}, in the plain machine and in the default switch set of the integration of 2026-11-24.}
\li{Since the fix the let variable carries the value of its declared type, and the machine rejects \code{\verb~|S.bad~}. The typed bindings of the related fixes cost nothing measurable: without them the steps change by -0.35 percent on the Cedar slice and -0.01 percent on Std.}
\li{The same pattern appeared in four more places, findings E1-F2 to E1-F5: the bound variable of a beta redex, the comparison variable of a lambda against a Pi, and two forms of the expected-type rule. All five were wrong accepts of true statements, found by new hostile exports; all five shapes now get the official verdict.}
}
\p{Used by [an evaluator that types values cannot match a kernel that types unreduced terms](ins-AAXM).}
\p{See also: [inference shortcuts and typed bindings](design-inference-shortcuts).}
